  "description": "openEHR Archetype Object Model (AOM2) for .NET: hand-authored,\n      polymorphic, mutable data classes covering identification helpers,\n      the Resource layer, the constraint hierarchy (C_OBJECT, C_ATTRIBUTE,\n      C_PRIMITIVE_OBJECT and friends), the terminology container, and the\n      Archetype/Template/OperationalTemplate roots. Ships the structural\n      surface only; the ADL2 parser/serializer lands in later phases.\n      Trim-safe and Native-AOT-safe. Single TFM net10.0.",
